# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads to Cloud Storage. gcloud does NOT read
# .dockerignore for this, and without this file it would fall back to
# .gitignore - so the private key's safety would depend on .gitignore never
# changing. Explicit allowlist instead: ignore everything, then let through
# only what the Dockerfile needs. .env and keys/private.pem stay out.
#
# Syntax is gitignore's: `*` matches at every depth, so re-including a
# directory needs both the directory and its contents (`src/` + `src/**`).
*
!Dockerfile
!.dockerignore
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!tsconfig.json
!src/
!src/**
!keys/
# gcloud treats `!keys/` as re-including the whole folder (unlike git), so
# exclude its contents again and let only the public key back in.
keys/*
!keys/public.pem
